          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "mongoexport defaults to Relaxed Extended JSON v2. Use --jsonFormat=canonical when BSON type fidelity matters; mongoimport recognizes Canonical input without a corresponding import-mode flag. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:8b13da6936e927e438c55ecdbe6bc43f83b5f2756169e728fd0da47b7022839f",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:2354b6011fd1fa43b5d6f6b98e453af42402e5820f2960340d87846cd4be4b57",
            "ev:c9ec4a02fa540181994b28031395456531b4b67a8c3d408601bfa0bf57dafb93"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "TideWave says Canonical JSON round-trips every type exactly. The Extended JSON specification explicitly limits arbitrary BSON round trips because of ordering and dollar-prefixed wrapper ambiguity; interpret the blog claim as guidance about explicit type representation, not a universal round-trip guarantee. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://tidewave.net/blog/importing-and-exporting-data-with-mongoimport-and-mongoexport",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4432e845856931f22a18d694d6425b07d5196b282428884b1ea0635a6d81c4f0",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:32767c2683058165d4514be276cafeb5b39d041321bb90d45cc4f62c8d7c724e",
            "ev:ba74263806cfd8043415a556f6efff2ac5dfa8f2c552c352a6210bdaf3a1346b"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/extended-json/extended-json.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Plain JSON directly represents only a subset of BSON types. Canonical Extended JSON emphasizes type preservation; Relaxed mode emphasizes readability and interoperability and can lose type information when converted to BSON. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cb86ccfde25b6857b4806f19aa570d5dc521f55c7802991b620a01754d30b962",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:fee12407360762a39f3768e1a8f578905638f1f0b18430c5032e9274eae073e4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "mongoexport normally writes one JSON document per MongoDB document; --jsonArray writes one enclosing array. The mongoimport --jsonArray option accepts that form and its reference documents an import limit of 16 MB or smaller. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoexport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:af6350d4a98f89bea1c934fbad5f4dd65b8d3c49947b691d87dc7f1419858f16",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9f24f5bef380c78959cd949ee593a81b7bab864e8684b8e31a193ffe5d1d6601",
            "ev:d11ec8afd344691bf797f05860d8ff0b0b93735c1fdf49d2673c1ae2f0d9c442"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "DRIVERS-3456 demonstrates a dollar-date field collision: an embedded document containing a date-looking string becomes a BSON Date after an Extended JSON round trip. This is an attributed encoding limitation, not evidence that every dollar-prefixed key corrupts data. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://jira.mongodb.org/browse/DRIVERS-3456",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:19a07208334dfb19682bc2ec40820eee8cae17a72cf10de535466c4998fcbafe",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:336861af54444dc167732d99dc75a02be01468d52bfd77b39841231c5c36e5ea",
            "ev:c9bf4ecaf5d8d52547a6be30f16d1eec1f1bf8c787db59453720bf67382ae439"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/extended-json/extended-json.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For CSV or TSV input, --headerline uses the first row as field names; otherwise mongoimport imports that row as a document. --headerline produces an error for JSON input. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:82b12d4a647b894487aea797fa45f5c36e09302373e74e20b45aaa90c9260022",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:776813e548f1180ab78b1f7df54eb2385d8cb1438a8dc51e223ba041f89058ac"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Extended JSON v2 cannot distinguish type-wrapper keys from user fields with the same names; DBRef is an exception to the documented warning about dollar-prefixed keys. In CSV, periods denote hierarchy, so a literal period in a field name can be misread as nesting. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9a82235f0d949cc5f76163c9fb80652be513eed3b1037fc03c1baaaa21ae05a2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:eb3f5bc2ea7888a0b62053e1d260a1aa6fd22991a5b9bf7fa3e0810fd4e14811"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "mongoexport CSV requires --fields or --fieldFile to select columns. It writes field names as a header by default; --noHeaderLine suppresses that header. Use mongoimport --headerline to consume a CSV or TSV header as names rather than data. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoexport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:dd8c979cee33fa3189dcce115c5316f2b50dd975dc134985241c98fca813a6ea",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0056a3623256ec87618b77dc83cf98531ed85e2ca398e82a592f9fee72a8fd3e",
            "ev:6875626c8b1c6a13c6c04643930b501dcef0d783cb04f11537788366678ee793",
            "ev:776813e548f1180ab78b1f7df54eb2385d8cb1438a8dc51e223ba041f89058ac"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Canonical Extended JSON is not an unconditional guarantee of arbitrary BSON document round trips: reserved dollar-prefixed field names can collide with type wrappers, and the specification also notes JSON object ordering differs from BSON ordering. CSV dots denote nesting and therefore can misinterpret literal dots in field names. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/extended-json/extended-json.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:62b51f246c01f60a92ba99a2e1705dce69b8543893ecf3142de6fe16d1dddfde",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:ba74263806cfd8043415a556f6efff2ac5dfa8f2c552c352a6210bdaf3a1346b",
            "ev:cf255b58caf129afcf0f351a5d679ee09ab4f6cc0f32d1fb6bd032b2db35c4bc"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Canonical Extended JSON preserves explicit numeric type information, whereas Relaxed Extended JSON uses ordinary JSON numbers for integers and finite doubles and can lose numeric type distinctions. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f31b6b7877690b0ed30bd3a11c9431a8294ee212753273a89bb72c854314983d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:172d1ac39ecfeb7b092703024afa8f5a5a6dab860c09713341e5c54e9bf509f1",
            "ev:2239378e04308d0b665922e6b6b9ff0683e4010824fb3564b4cb04d921f6fc5b"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/extended-json/extended-json.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Extended JSON uses a $oid wrapper for ObjectId and a $numberDecimal wrapper for Decimal128 in both Canonical and Relaxed modes. Relaxed mode does not remove every BSON type wrapper. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f83625d6b72f48e0aa59418d531c9b9d99ab773dbdebb5c9b7a08ff18b57a2a8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:7299cf30550134a726cb6db98928e3b9b72fd931fa1bf06537516453b0dddd80",
            "ev:a793ee4df52eedb2e1dc3e0cc1be5e8c258781daeaccb1098163bae1328d103e"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "mongoimport expects Extended JSON v2 Canonical or Relaxed input by default; use --legacy for Extended JSON v1 input. Legacy regular-expression representations can otherwise be interpreted as ordinary embedded documents. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fac3f3afd45bcb7ff267cec8e2455027e80ef3406cebda6591b2e60c5471209c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:05282e92016d4726998ada3b1898406133dc93d2990fc78483b880a414dad807",
            "ev:f4b90d6225231de6c7891cc990f468fcd1a890a7ffebb37a5585896951a73881"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
            "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/user-guide/compatibility-changes-in-mongodb-4-2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CSV and TSV do not carry BSON type metadata. Use --columnsHaveTypes with typed fields from --fields, --fieldFile or --headerline; declarations can select string(), int32(), int64(), double(), decimal(), boolean() and date formats. The option does not apply to JSON input. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:c9a1675597b8c834613603a6f64fe5630842c5d0c72a35df0a7a2b8c4dcb8f0a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5b35a8a7835f647dc63a94ceb1ca421065f3afa94f56e8e9bda5ef3e46ef73fe",
            "ev:8b039e636ef67841f0566f763e126af9ead20a45273aef71127099732d46fba0"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-guide.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For typed CSV dates, date(<arg>) aliases date_go(<arg>) and uses a Go reference-time layout. An ISO-looking cell alone is insufficient: a reported import with an empty date() argument failed type coercion, and the answer supplied a layout template. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e287366d6da190b5afdb038bd2750bcc119a8ab4551181c7e669ea94f65047f7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:9d83268567359d5ab6c65a1d762b68f148bc9d81414ef496297e0f315ed70c56",
            "ev:e15ddac362fffc1a731b27aad693e8806f380dc94307f784ae6460e6dfcc7c69",
            "ev:e7f42510fbe1884bedb36a5880f380827917d70cc60ce23b24099e93c5ece800"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://stackoverflow.com/questions/43676853/importing-csv-file-mongodb-with-isodate"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "mongoimport only supports UTF-8 input files; other encodings produce errors. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:057d458f691d83b26b8570cdf200301a214fa19b8dc09d9599f6ea88c41e340d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1f0baa05225f5f0cce2e8d5cddb2133926090a958898e9cb92fc924cf0cfb872"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The tool reference and the TideWave guide disagree about the default --parseGrace setting: the reference says stop, while TideWave labels autoCast as the default. Treat the reference as authoritative; explicitly choose a policy for typed CSV/TSV coercion failures. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:78921f6bb43952d829d51a9b079709d5a4c36db4ad4daafe2f32ea55b867a3da",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:180921784774d9dec207daf19057e61b6f4cefbd6eeb0d0b6abf9f34c68a837c",
            "ev:ca90453e82511bcaf1d09c2d39f1a644ff71c94446c7a673da582d8057802ff5"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://tidewave.net/blog/importing-and-exporting-data-with-mongoimport-and-mongoexport"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "mongoexport defaults to Extended JSON v2 Relaxed mode. Set --jsonFormat=canonical to produce Canonical mode. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0d4ed3593dfd2ae707611d89099bdc08cd91695c6550f0c047323ec7b7ba2b1d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:a7d9fc9494d7c173ac7cea34078566c48878838f156ea8768a5beee130000e22",
            "ev:a96fcb7ed938b16ae63f679746906f38269ec5d3f1e7b9186dfdd4443b3f2d96"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/user-guide/compatibility-changes-in-mongodb-4-2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For rich BSON type preservation in JSON interchange, use Canonical Extended JSON. mongoimport recognizes the format in the input file, including Canonical output from mongoexport. This recommendation remains subject to field-name and Extended JSON representation restrictions. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-behavior.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a5c33f2995cb47cf713c931f50ed2edf9fd33c65fd1e31d3b7ec3c276621fa18",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4110262729d62a00f564c611d37aedf2fe0772ba433a628419662f835d5c9569",
            "ev:f9bd6876d348a0e9ee93c6c7e0203bdaa0cc407a4e8d828e4fa935724c45fd89"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Canonical Extended JSON represents BSON integer types with $numberInt and $numberLong string-valued wrappers. Relaxed mode represents them as JSON integer values, so the representation does not retain that integer-width distinction. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/mongodb-extended-json.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:a792bbbb077586c144223f5b58033b74984a16d21e648fedf40907217944da7a",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:37eccb3a732bbe69c911bbbc4e822f021bcad17b1805c5667f81b95b45be2561"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CSV export requires an explicit field list through --fields or --fieldFile. mongoexport includes a CSV header by default; --noHeaderLine suppresses it and is valid only for CSV output. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoexport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e1946d526c8404d7e7d9a8211641bbe488157b77b2382bfe7a640f02b385adba",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0056a3623256ec87618b77dc83cf98531ed85e2ca398e82a592f9fee72a8fd3e",
            "ev:828fbe1f4fe35ae8fbbf4a4bc0ff48a763091a31eea31ad01da977ac800bc89b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CSV and TSV can carry explicit import types: combine --columnsHaveTypes with --fields, --fieldFile, or --headerline and specify each field as <colName>.<type>(<arg>). --columnsHaveTypes is invalid for JSON input. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-examples.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:cb6c53ae1e7e60a4d250ee1c3bcb0e454e1ba4fd1945ef9e43937ac3ad4cfb75",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3efc2083bfd308054e6c53cb34ac8ac1db7e576e2041ce6866a25d2673706800",
            "ev:8f7c7ca1bf368686ee9fcf0244a1d337c79432b51f11c5a87fb6feb1d0f2d610"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For typed CSV imports, date() uses the Go time.Parse layout. The official example specifies birthdate.date(2006-01-02), alongside string(), boolean(), int32(), and binary(base64) fields. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f71c0f50a9a11bf119315fe49e017954e3e74c9fbf80cd2456d33cd0f3db47b3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:6b08b3860537faa24466bacb46fb3009e11bcd676d0ccc55f9d9d3a921c8718a",
            "ev:e7f42510fbe1884bedb36a5880f380827917d70cc60ce23b24099e93c5ece800"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport/mongoimport-examples.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For CSV or TSV type-coercion failures with --columnsHaveTypes, --parseGrace defaults to stop. Alternatives are autoCast, skipField, and skipRow; autoCast can change the resulting field type. --parseGrace has no effect for JSON input. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/database-tools/mongoimport.md",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:14bb43fafd929869fbdc2a35bd04847da82d2a40d140cfeffa73c69426925095",
